 "reading": {
  "q1_completed": "the hidden surface is now measured in BYTES per vendor: the facade asks about N% of the varstore bytes it declares; the rest is policy the UI never surfaces (the variable-level hiding ring 19 predicted)",
  "the_setup_blob": "the per-vendor Setup varstore row prices the classic setup_var target: size, covered bytes, uncovered bytes, question count"
 },
 "honesty": [
  "question width is 1 byte by default; ONE_OF takes its widest option type, STRING/PASSWORD count 2 bytes (one utf-16 char — dynamic lengths unknown), NUMERIC width needs the raw flags byte the dissection did not retain (recorded as 1 — an undercount, i.e. uncovered shares are UPPER bounds on hiding)",
  "coverage unions intervals per varstore; overlapping questions collapse (the union is the honest measure)",
  "name_value varstores carry no size (offset-keyed) — excluded from byte totals, counted in varstore_count",
  "HII anchor scans over PE + RAW sections only; forms packages living elsewhere would be missed (the exact-consumption rule keeps what is found honest)",
  "the gate reproduces ring 19's totals under the same grammar — a grammar divergence would fail loudly, not silently re-base"
 ]
